\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou gracious God, whose mercy lends
\par The light of home, the smile of friends,
\par Our gathered flock Thine arms enfold,
\par As in the peaceful days of old.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Wilt Thou not hear us while we raise,
\par In sweet accord of solemn praise,
\par The voices that have mingled long
\par The joyous flow of mirth and song?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For all the blessings life has brought,
\par For all its sorrowing hours have taught,
\par For all we mourn, for all we keep,
\par The hands we clasp, the loved that sleep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The noontide sunshine of the past,
\par These brief, bright moments fading fast,
\par The stars that glid our darkening years,
\par The twilight ray from holier spheres.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. We thank Thee, Father; let Thy grace
\par Our loving circle still embrace,
\par Thy mercy shed its heavenly store,
\par Thy peace be with us evermore.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

